Share all your campus events and activities on the SU System Master Calendar!
The Office of External Affairs and University Relations maintains an online Master Calendar to include all official University events and activities throughout the System.
The SU System Master Calendar lists all events and activities and provide instant, online access&nbsp;to&nbsp;a&nbsp;centralized&nbsp;calendar&nbsp;of&nbsp;events&nbsp;that provides&nbsp;date,&nbsp;time&nbsp;and&nbsp;location,&nbsp;event&nbsp;description, directions to the venue, and other important information.
Please submit any official campus events and activities, including athletic and alumni events by using the following link to share information electronically:&nbsp;<a href="http://www.sus.edu/form/su-system-master-calendar-submission" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">http://www.sus.edu/form/su-system-master-calendar-submission</a>
&nbsp;

The Southern University System Foundation is calling on all Southern University alumni, students, faculty, staff, and supporters to unite for its annual SU Give Day on Thursday, Aug. 27. This all-day virtual event, streamed live on <a id="OWAa6c8f4bb-cc88-d541-93f4-7b418c4cd84e" class="OWAAutoLink" title="https://www.facebook.com/southernuniversitybatonrouge" href="https://www.facebook.com/southernuniversitybatonrouge" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-auth="NotApplicable" data-linkindex="0" data-ogsc=""><u>Southern's Facebook page</u></a>, is the final appeal for the Foundation’s “Are You In?” campaign. This year's goal is $25 million.
&nbsp;
The goal is to rally support and secure philanthropic contributions for Southern's five campuses — Southern University and A&amp;M College, Southern University at New Orleans, Southern University Shreveport, Southern University Law Center, and Southern University Agricultural Research and Extension Center — as well as the Southern University Laboratory School.
&nbsp;
From 9 a.m. to 6 p.m., SU Give Day will feature a series of panel discussions and presentations, hosted by Cumulus Media on-air personality LaTangela Sherman, live from the Valdry Center for Philanthropy on the Baton Rouge campus. The schedule includes:
&nbsp;
For more information or to make a contribution, go to <a id="OWA7576fd1a-b1d6-1045-15bf-da78e4a9610d" class="OWAAutoLink" title="http://sugiveday.org" href="http://sugiveday.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-auth="NotApplicable" data-linkindex="1" data-ogsc="">sugiveday.org</a>.
